A. DATA ACCURACY
-------------------------------------------------------------

1. LATA totals are incorrect (P1)
   Issue: The statewide panel shows 0 LATA projects and $0. County and district panels show a static value (about $550K) for every area.
   Action: Connect the statewide panel to the LATA data and calculate the area values from the LATA fields per geography. CPUC will provide QC'd LATA data after confirming with the LATA team.
   Done when: Statewide LATA count and amount match the source data, and area values differ by geography.

2. FFA statewide project count (P1)
   Issue: The statewide panel shows 120 FFA projects. The expected count is 123.
   Action: Update the count once CPUC confirms which project list to use.
   Done when: The count matches the CPUC-confirmed figure.

3. Statewide totals count each project once (P1)
   Action: Calculate statewide figures from the source project data, not by summing county or district values (multi-area projects would be double-counted).

-------------------------------------------------------------
B. MAP DESIGN
-------------------------------------------------------------

4. Default view and mask (P1) – in progress
   Action: Set the starting extent to California. Mask or gray out all areas outside California.

5. Basemap (P2)
   Action: Replace the terrain basemap with the MMBI basemap used on the FFA Awards map, so the two products match.

6. Selection highlight (P2)
   Issue: Selected areas show only an outline, the zoom is too tight, and the highlight works on some layers but not others.
   Action: Add a highlight fill and outline, add padding around the zoomed extent, and keep surrounding counties or districts visible.
   Done when: The highlight looks the same on the County, Assembly and Senate layers.

7. Labels (P2)
   Action: Add county and district labels at zoomed-in scales. Labels are hidden at the statewide scale to avoid clutter.

8. Layer colors (P2)
   Action:
   - Assign LATA its own color. Gray reads as "no data."
   - Change the Tribal Areas color so it is clearly distinguishable. Do not use red.
   - Use a colorblind-safe palette across all program colors, and do not rely on color alone (also use labels or patterns).

9. Remove the State Boundary layer (P3)
   Action: Remove it from the layer list. It has no visible effect, and the county and district layers already show the state outline.

-------------------------------------------------------------
C. DETAILS PANEL – CONTENT AND LAYOUT
-------------------------------------------------------------

10. Rename "District Details" (P2)
    Action: Use the geography type in the header, for example "County Details – Alameda" or "Senate District 5 Details." A county is not a district.

11. Rename "Overall Projects" (P2)
    Action: Change to "Total Projects" to match "Total Investment."

12. Consistent program names (P2)
    Action: Use the same full program names in every panel and write out all acronyms:
    - Federal Funding Account
    - California Advanced Services Fund (CASF) Public Housing
    - CASF Broadband Adoption
    - Local Agency Technical Assistance (LATA)

13. Match the details panel layout to the statewide summary (P2)
    Action: Use the same layout, order, font sizes and number formatting for the area details as for the statewide overview. Align the project details design with the area details, and adjust the individual program descriptions.

14. Methodology note (P1)
    Action: Add an info icon next to the details header that opens a methodology pop-up with this text:
    "Details are calculated as the number of projects and their award amounts that fall within the boundaries of the selected geography. Because projects may cross multiple geographies, some projects and their funding may be counted in more than one geography. Statewide totals count each project once."

15. Selector dropdowns (P2)
    Action: Show the full name for the selected value, for example "Senate District 4" or "Assembly District 12." Abbreviations (SD 4, AD 12) are fine in the dropdown list itself.

16. Details section size (P2)
    Action: Enlarge the details section using the space freed up by item 22.

-------------------------------------------------------------
D. TEXT, FORMATTING AND ACCESSIBILITY
-------------------------------------------------------------

17. Font sizes and contrast (P2)
    Action: Standardize font sizes across the app and make all text meet WCAG 2.1 AA:
    - Text contrast at least 4.5:1
    - Body text at least 14px, with no text below 12px (including the project count badges)
    - Fix plural labels ("1 Project," not "1 Projects")

18. Currency format (P2) – final rule to be confirmed by CPUC
    Proposed rule: Round to whole thousands below $1M ($599K, $403K). Use one decimal for millions and billions ($74.9M, $1.2B). Apply the same rule everywhere.

